{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5iqnZRALP2D8Nt6DkYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\nLooking at existing patterns in ShipmentControllerTest.kt and OrderControllerTest.kt:\n- Controllers throw `ConflictException` for HTTP 409 (state conflict)\n- Controllers throw `ResourceNotFoundException` for HTTP 404 (missing resource)  \n- ErrorCode enum defines machine-readable codes for each error scenario\n- Tests assert both status code AND error response body (code, message)\n- Controllers return domain objects directly; Spring serializes via Jackson\n- MockMvc tests use jsonPath assertions on response body\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Must add new ErrorCode `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` for the 409 case when confirming a CANCELLED shipment. This is the only shared infrastructure file touched, required by the confirm operation's error contract.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add the confirm endpoint (`POST /{shipmentId}/confirm`). Handles the three cases: CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→idempotent success, CANCELLED→ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE.\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add four test cases: confirm CREATED succeeds with status 200 and returns CONFIRMED shipment; confirm CONFIRMED is idempotent; confirm CANCELLED returns 409 with error code; confirm unknown returns 404 with error code.\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Idempotency bug: if confirm CONFIRMED overwrites state, causing loss of audit trail or state inconsistency\n- Error code missing: if SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE not added, ConflictException will fail at runtime\n- Endpoint signature mismatch: if the path pattern doesn't match Spring's expectation\n- Regression: if existing create/read/list tests break due to controller changes\n\n**Open questions:** None—all four cases (CREATED, CONFIRMED idempotent, CANCELLED, not found) are fully specified.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum, after SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS. This codes the case where a shipment is in a state incompatible with the requested operation (e.g., CANCELLED when trying to confirm).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new POST endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   The logic:\n   - Look up the shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException (404) if not found\n   - Check the status: \n     - If CREATED: update to CONFIRMED, save, return the updated shipment with 200\n     - If CONFIRMED: return the shipment as-is with 200 (idempotent)\n     - If CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n   - Return the shipment directly (Spring serializes to JSON)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and returns it with status 200` — create S-1 with CREATED, call confirm, assert 200 and status=CONFIRMED\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment without changing it` — create S-2 with CREATED, confirm twice, assert both succeed and status remains CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` — write S-3 with CANCELLED directly to repo, call confirm, assert 409 with error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - `rejects confirming an unknown shipment with 404` — call confirm on S-unknown, assert 404 with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nCould I avoid adding SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE by reusing ConflictException with a different error code? No—the existing codes (SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) don't fit the semantic of \"shipment is in an invalid state for this operation.\" A new code is required to maintain the API's contract of machine-readable error codes that clients can branch on.\n\nCould the confirm endpoint be a PUT or PATCH instead of POST? No—the requirement explicitly says `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`, and POST is idiomatic for state-change actions that are not full replacement.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | HTTP | Response body |\n|------|------|-------|------|---------------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | Find by ID; found | Update status to CONFIRMED, save | 200 | Updated Shipment |\n| CONFIRMED→idempotent | Find by ID; found | No write | 200 | Existing Shipment |\n| CANCELLED | Find by ID; found | No write | 409 | ApiError {code: SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, message} |\n| Not found | Find by ID; not found | No write | 404 | ApiError {code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message} |\n\nThe repository's `save()` method returns the saved shipment; the controller returns it directly. Spring's GlobalExceptionHandler catches ApiException subclasses and wraps them in the error envelope.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirm CREATED shipment** — Verifies the happy path: a freshly created shipment transitions to CONFIRMED and is persisted.\n2. **Test: confirm CONFIRMED shipment twice** — Verifies idempotency: calling confirm twice on an already-CONFIRMED shipment succeeds both times without error or state change.\n3. **Test: confirm CANCELLED shipment** — Verifies conflict rejection: a shipment in CANCELLED state cannot be confirmed; returns 409 with the SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code.\n4. **Test: confirm unknown shipment** — Verifies not-found rejection: confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code.\n\nEach test:\n- Sets up the fixture (create shipment or write directly to repo for CANCELLED)\n- Calls the confirm endpoint via MockMvc POST\n- Asserts status code, error code (if applicable), and shipment state in response body\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4092,"cache_read_input_tokens":17699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4092},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7827047-f100-48af-b053-dbd7b8ddc410","uuid":"01213276-b963-4194-a2b5-d27d32ac3f91","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:46:53.083Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5iqn7szGw5ANE6aGYb1"}
