nd \"shipment in wrong state to confirm\" (409). The existing code set did not cover this case.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` method:\n   - Correctly handles all four cases from the requirement\n   - CREATED → saves updated state, returns 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - CONFIRMED → returns existing state unchanged, 200 (idempotent)\n   - CANCELLED → throws ConflictException with new SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code, 409\n   - Not found → throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code, 404\n   - Uses repository.save() and repository.findById() consistently with existing patterns\n   - Endpoint path `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` matches requirement\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added four test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment...` — happy path\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment...` — idempotency\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment...` — state conflict\n   - `rejects confirming an unknown shipment...` — not found\n   - All tests follow existing test pattern: MockMvc.perform(), status assertions, jsonPath body checks\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add an idempotent POST endpoint to confirm a shipment, moving it from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, while rejecting invalid state transitions and unknown shipments.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `ApiError.kt` — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` ErrorCode for 409 shipment state conflicts\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — Added `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint with state machine: CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→idempotent, CANCELLED→409, not found→404\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added 4 test cases covering: confirm CREATED, confirm CONFIRMED (idempotent), confirm CANCELLED (409), confirm unknown (404)\n\n**Tests:**\n- `confirms a created shipment and returns it with status CONFIRMED` — Verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition persists and returns updated shipment\n- `co